.TH sys_fs_cgroup 5 (date) "Linux man-pages (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
/sys/fs/cgroup/ \- mount points for cgroups filesystems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /sys/fs/cgroup/
.SH DESCRIPTION
This directory conventionally is used as a mount point for a
.BR tmpfs (5)
filesystem containing mount points for
.BR cgroups (7)
filesystems.
.SH STANDARDS
Linux.
.SH HISTORY
Linux 2.6.0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_fs (5)
